## Lessons for Other Polymarket Traders

Golgatha's approach offers several insights for traders at any experience level. First, selectivity can outperform activity. The temptation on [Polymarket](https://polymarket.com/?r=POLYTips) is to engage with every trending market, but spreading capital thin often leads to mediocre results across the board. Golgatha demonstrates that finding one market where you possess genuine informational or analytical edge can be more valuable than participating in fifty markets where your edge is marginal. Second, the psychological discipline required to trade only one market while others chase headlines is itself a competitive advantage. Most traders overtrade, and the transaction costs and cognitive errors accumulate. Third, Golgatha's record suggests the value of waiting for fat pitches. In prediction markets, odds fluctuate constantly, and patience allows a trader to enter only when the expected value is most favorable. This approach may mean sitting out for weeks or months, but the returns justify the inactivity.

